---@class posthog.stamphog.CreateStamphogRepoConfigRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field provider? string SCM provider this config talks to. Defaults to 'github'.
---@field repository string Repository full name, e.g. 'PostHog/posthog'.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether stamphog actively reviews pull requests for this repo.
---@field digest_enabled? boolean Whether merged PRs on this repo are captured for the daily Slack digest.
---@field review_mode? posthog.stamphog.ReviewModeEnum|string When reviews run: 'label' reviews only pull requests carrying the trigger label (the default), mirroring the Action's opt-in flow; 'all' reviews every pull request. * `all` - All pull requests * `label` - Labeled pull requests
---@field trigger_label? string Pull request label that triggers a review when review_mode is 'label'. Defaults to 'stamphog'.
---@field routing_mode? posthog.stamphog.RoutingModeEnum|string When stamphog requests reviews from the code owners in the repository's owners.yaml: 'off' (the default) never; 'always' when a pull request opens ready for review or is marked ready; 'fallback' only when stamphog does not approve, where an approval requests only the owners of sensitive and new paths. * `off` - Off * `always` - Always * `fallback` - When stamphog does not approve
---@field routing_fork_labels? posthog.stamphog.CreateStamphogRepoConfigRequestRoutingForkLabelsMap On fork pull requests, routing adds the mapped label instead of requesting a review from the team, so an outside author cannot notify it. Keys are owners.yaml team slugs such as 'team-devex', values are GitHub label names. A team with no entry gets a review request as usual. Sending the field replaces the whole map, and an empty object removes every label.

