---@field merged boolean Whether this pull request has merged (merged_at is set).
---@field merged_at string|distilled.Null When the pull request merged, null if it hasn't.
---@field merge_commit_sha string Merge commit SHA, blank until the pull request merges.
---@field additions number Lines added, recorded when the pull request merges.
---@field deletions number Lines deleted, recorded when the pull request merges.
---@field changed_files number Files changed, recorded when the pull request merges.
---@field routing_mode posthog.stamphog.RoutingModeEnum The repository's routing_mode now. 'off' means reviewer routing does not run for new events. * `off` - Off * `always` - Always * `fallback` - When stamphog does not approve
---@field routing posthog.stamphog.StamphogPullRequestRouting|distilled.Null The latest reviewer routing record of the pull request, or null when routing never wrote one: routing is off, the pull request is still a draft, or no routing event arrived yet. Use the routing runs list for the owners each run requested or cut.
---@field created_at string When this pull request was first captured.
---@field updated_at string When this pull request was last updated.

---@class posthog.stamphog.StamphogPullRequestRouting
---@field status posthog.stamphog.RoutingStatusEnum The phase of the latest routing record: 'waiting' (fallback mode, the head waits for stamphog's verdict or the safety net), 'routing' (a task holds the claim and requested nobody yet), 'requested' (the review requests went out, the routing comment is not finished) or 'done'. * `waiting` - Waiting for stamphog's verdict * `routing` - Routing * `requested` - Requested * `done` - Done
---@field mode posthog.stamphog.RoutingModeEnum The repository's routing_mode when the record was written. Compare with the pull request's routing_mode. * `off` - Off * `always` - Always * `fallback` - When stamphog does not approve
---@field scope posthog.stamphog.RoutingScopeEnum|distilled.Null 'full', or 'pinned' when a stamphog approval asks only the owners of sensitive and new paths. Null while the record waits. * `full` - Every owner * `pinned` - Pinned owners only
---@field head_sha string The head commit the record is for. It can be older than the pull request head.
---@field trigger string What started the record: 'opened', 'ready_for_review', 'verdict:<outcome>' or 'safety_net'.
---@field claim_expired boolean True when a 'routing' or 'requested' claim is older than the takeover limit. The task can still be alive, and a later delivery does not always finish an expired 'requested' claim.
---@field waiting_since string|distilled.Null When the head started to wait for stamphog's verdict. Null unless waiting.
---@field claimed_at string|distilled.Null When a task claimed the pull request for this record.
---@field routed_at string|distilled.Null When the claim planned its requests. Null until the plan is saved.
---@field full_routed_head string The head that a full routing of this pull request requested owners for, blank if none. Fallback mode routes in full at most once per pull request.
---@field pinned_routed_head string The latest approved head whose pinned owners were requested, blank if none.

---@class posthog.stamphog.StamphogRepoConfig
---@field id string
---@field provider? string SCM provider this config talks to. Defaults to 'github'.
---@field repository string Repository full name, e.g. 'PostHog/posthog'.
---@field enabled boolean Whether stamphog actively reviews pull requests for this repo.
---@field installation_id string Provider app installation ID that authorizes API calls for this repo. Set only by the verified sync_installation flow; ignored on direct writes.
---@field digest_enabled? boolean Whether merged PRs on this repo are captured for the daily Slack digest. Requires 'enabled', since the digest reports what stamphog approved.
---@field review_mode posthog.stamphog.ReviewModeEnum When reviews run: 'label' reviews only pull requests carrying the trigger label (the default), mirroring the Action's opt-in flow; 'all' reviews every pull request. * `all` - All pull requests * `label` - Labeled pull requests
---@field trigger_label? string Pull request label that triggers a review when review_mode is 'label'. Defaults to 'stamphog'.
---@field routing_mode posthog.stamphog.RoutingModeEnum When stamphog requests reviews from the code owners in the repository's owners.yaml: 'off' (the default) never; 'always' when a pull request opens ready for review or is marked ready; 'fallback' only when stamphog does not approve, where an approval requests only the owners of sensitive and new paths. * `off` - Off * `always` - Always * `fallback` - When stamphog does not approve
---@field routing_fork_labels posthog.stamphog.StamphogRepoConfigRoutingForkLabelsMap On fork pull requests, routing adds the mapped label instead of requesting a review from the team, so an outside author cannot notify it. Keys are owners.yaml team slugs such as 'team-devex', values are GitHub label names. A team with no entry gets a review request as usual.
---@field user_access_level string|distilled.Null The caller's access level on the stamphog resource, resolved for the team that owns this row. 'editor' can turn reviews on. 'manager' is required to turn them off or to change review_mode, trigger_label, routing_mode or routing_fork_labels.
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string

---On fork pull requests, routing adds the mapped label instead of requesting a review from the team, so an outside author cannot notify it. Keys are owners.yaml team slugs such as 'team-devex', values are GitHub label names. A team with no entry gets a review request as usual.
