---@class posthog.stamphog.StamphogRoutingFile
---@field path string The changed path.
---@field previous_path? string|distilled.Null The path before a rename. Null for any other change.
---@field status? string GitHub's file status, such as 'added', 'modified', 'removed' or 'renamed'.
---@field additions? number Added lines.
---@field deletions? number Deleted lines.
---@field owners_source? string|distilled.Null Repo-relative path of the ownership file, read at the run's owners_sha, whose `owners` list names this owner for the file. Null when only an additions declaration made the owner a candidate (see the owner's `new_path` pins), or when the run is older than this field.

---@class posthog.stamphog.StamphogRoutingPin
---@field reason posthog.stamphog.PinReasonEnum Why the path pins its owner. * `sensitive` - Sensitive path * `new_path` - New path
---@field path string The changed path, or the new directory, that pinned the owner.

---@class posthog.stamphog.StamphogRoutingRun
---@field id string ID of the routing run.
---@field repository string Full name of the repository.
---@field pr_number number Pull request number.
---@field head_sha string The head commit the run routed.
---@field mode posthog.stamphog.RoutingModeEnum The repository's routing_mode when the run made its requests. * `off` - Off * `always` - Always * `fallback` - When stamphog does not approve
---@field trigger string What started the run: 'opened', 'ready_for_review', 'verdict:<outcome>' or 'safety_net'.
---@field scope posthog.stamphog.RoutingScopeEnum 'full', or 'pinned' when a stamphog approval asked only the owners of sensitive and new paths. * `full` - Every owner * `pinned` - Pinned owners only
---@field fork? boolean Whether the pull request came from a fork, which skips the model.
---@field llm_skipped posthog.stamphog.LlmSkipReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why the cut step made no model call. Null when it made one. * `single_candidate` - Single candidate * `fork` - Fork * `nothing_cuttable` - Nothing cuttable * `no_answer` - No answer * `stamphog_approved` - Stamphog approved * `files_truncated` - Files truncated
---@field model? string The model the cut request reached. Blank when no request reached the gateway.
---@field files_truncated? boolean Whether GitHub listed fewer files than the pull request changes, so owners may be missing.
---@field additions_resolved? boolean Whether the new-path lookup worked. When false, owners of new paths may not be pinned.
