---@field reason posthog.stamphog.RoutingOwnerReasonEnum Why: 'sensitive' or 'new_path' (pinned, never cut), 'largest_owner' (a pull request keeps at least one reviewer), 'diff_not_seen' (the model did not see all of the owner's diff), 'cut_skipped' (no model call, see llm_skipped on the run), 'model_kept', 'model_cut' or 'stamphog_approved'. * `sensitive` - Owns a sensitive path * `new_path` - Owns a new path * `largest_owner` - Has the largest part * `diff_not_seen` - Diff not shown to the model * `cut_skipped` - Cut step skipped * `model_kept` - Kept by the model * `model_cut` - Cut by the model * `stamphog_approved` - Stamphog approved
